# Cloudflare Pages redirects.
#
# DELIBERATELY SHORT. Every URL the live site currently ranks for is regenerated
# at its exact existing path by the new build, so almost nothing needs
# redirecting:
#
#   /                                  -> unchanged
#   /about /services                   -> unchanged
#   /contact /privacy /terms /blog     -> unchanged
#   /portfolio /pricing                -> temporarily redirected, see below
#   /thank-you                         -> unchanged
#   /blog-*  (15 posts)                -> unchanged, see src/pages/[legacySlug].astro
#
# Cloudflare Pages already 308-redirects the `.html` forms (/about.html ->
# /about) on its own, and `build.format: 'file'` keeps that behaviour identical
# to today. Adding explicit .html rules here would only create redirect chains.

# TEMPORARILY OFFLINE — case studies and pricing.
#
# The pages still exist in the repo (src/pages/_portfolio*, _pricing.astro) but
# the underscore prefix keeps Astro from building them, so there is no document
# at these paths. Without these rules the URLs would 404, which tells Google to
# drop them permanently — and both are indexed today.
#
# 302, not 301, because the intent is to bring them back. A 302 keeps the
# original URL in Google's index and transfers nothing away from it; a 301
# would hand the ranking to the destination and be cached by browsers, making
# the takedown much harder to reverse.
#
# TO RESTORE: drop the `_` prefixes, re-add the nav entries in src/consts.ts and
# the footer, and delete this block.
/portfolio                 /services           302
/portfolio/*               /services           302
/case-studies              /services           302
/case-studies/*            /services           302
/pricing                   /contact            302

# Convenience aliases for the primary offer — worth having for print, email
# signatures and anything typed by hand.
/audit                     /analyze            301
/free-audit                /analyze            301
/speed-test                /analyze            301
/pagespeed                 /analyze            301

# The legacy sitemap listed .html URLs that Cloudflare already redirects. This
# one is listed explicitly because the root form is ambiguous.
/index.html                /                   301

# Services retired in the Aug 2026 catalogue rework. Nothing published linked
# them, but they existed in a build, so point them at their nearest successor
# rather than serving a 404.
/services/core-web-vitals            /services/website-performance-optimization   301
/services/website-speed-optimization /services/website-performance-optimization   301
/services/conversion-optimization    /services/website-redesign                   301
